.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-DEBUG-BUNDLE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-debug-bundle
.Nd gather what it takes to diagnose a kldload machine into one tarball, secrets left out
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -out Ar dir
.Op Fl -quiet
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
collects, into one compressed tarball, the state that a diagnosis of a
kldload machine starts from:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
kldload's identity files, the list of what is in
.Pa /etc/kldload ,
the host id, and the kernel command line with any password values
removed;
.It
hardware: PCI devices and their drivers, loaded modules, the system's
DMI tables, CPU, memory and block devices;
.It
the installer's and kldload's logs,
.Pa /var/log/installer
and
.Pa /var/log/kldload ;
.It
the kernel log and the journal of this boot and the one before, and the
state of every unit;
.It
Secure Boot, the enrolled and pending machine owner keys, the SBAT
revocations, the EFI boot entries and the EFI partition's files;
.It
every pool's topology and properties, and every dataset's;
.It
DKMS: what is built, and the build log of any module that failed;
.It
module options and blacklists, and the X server's configuration;
.It
addresses, routes, DNS and NetworkManager's view;
.It
the installer's answers, and the public half of the module signing key.
.El
.Pp
It leaves out: the signing key's private half, WireGuard's keys, the ssh
host keys, the shadow password files, and the secrets under
.Pa /etc/kldload
\(em the root ssh key, the web console's token, the CA's private key,
the ZFS passphrase \(em which are copied by an allowlist, never the whole
directory.
Every
.Pa .env ,
.Pa .conf
and
.Pa .cfg
file in the bundle has any value whose name contains
.Ql PASS ,
.Ql PASSWORD ,
.Ql PASSPHRASE ,
.Ql SECRET ,
.Ql TOKEN ,
.Ql KEY
or
.Ql CREDENTIAL
replaced by
.Ql <redacted> .
.Pp
The tarball is created readable by root alone.
It changes nothing on the machine.
It must run as root; run as a user it re-executes itself with
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -out Ar dir
Write the tarball in
.Ar dir
instead of
.Pa /root .
.It Fl -quiet
Do not name each section on standard error as it is collected.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /root/kldload-debug- Ns Ar host Ns Pa - Ns Ar YYYYMMDD-HHMMSSZ Ns Pa .tar.gz
The bundle, mode 0600.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 2n -compact
.It 0
Written.
.It 64
A usage error.
.It 66
The output directory does not exist.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30; the bundle was removed
afterwards.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-debug-bundle --out /var/tmp/dbgtest-3609855
  kldload + system identity
  hardware (lspci, lsmod, /proc/{cpuinfo,meminfo})
  install-time logs (/var/log/installer)
  dmesg + journalctl (current + previous boot)
  Secure Boot / MOK / EFI
  ZFS pools, datasets, props
  DKMS modules
  modprobe + xorg config (nouveau-blacklist class of bugs)
  network state
  installer answers (passwords redacted)
  redacting secrets in every *.env/*.conf/*.cfg in the bundle
  compressing → /var/tmp/dbgtest-3609855/kldload-debug-onyx-20260930-071448Z.tar.gz

kldload-debug-bundle written: /var/tmp/dbgtest-3609855/kldload-debug-onyx-20260930-071448Z.tar.gz (65MB)
Inspect with: tar -tzf /var/tmp/dbgtest-3609855/kldload-debug-onyx-20260930-071448Z.tar.gz | head -40
Extract with: mkdir x && tar -C x -xzf /var/tmp/dbgtest-3609855/kldload-debug-onyx-20260930-071448Z.tar.gz
.Ed
.Pp
It took two minutes: the pool had 2,100 snapshots, whose properties are
all collected.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldload-debug-bundle --out
--out needs a directory
# (exited 64)
$ kldload-debug-bundle --out /nonexistent
output dir does not exist: /nonexistent
# (exited 66)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr journalctl 1 ,
.Xr kldload-doctor 8 ,
.Xr kldload-sysdiag 8
.Sh HISTORY
Until 2026-09-23 the bundle copied
.Pa /etc/kldload
whole, and with it the root ssh key, WireGuard keys, the web console's
token, the CA's private key and the ZFS passphrase; and it redacted two
answer names by list.
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: settings files were still copied raw
beside their redacted copies, the tarball was readable by anyone until it
was
.Xr chmod 1 Ns -ed ,
and it claimed to take about three seconds.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Logs and the journal are included as they are; a program that wrote a
secret to one of them sends it on in the bundle.
Read the bundle before handing it on.
.Pp
The time and size grow with the number of snapshots.
